# Every file has an owner, and today that owner is one person.
#
# `docs/decisions/0004-production-release.md` records that separation of duty is NOT achieved
# for release approval: one person is technical authority, quality authority and accepting
# party. This file states the same fact for code review rather than implying a second reviewer
# exists. When one does, the paths that most deserve a second pair of eyes are listed
# separately below so they can be reassigned first.

*                                   @Quitetall

# The authority kernel and the boundaries built on it. A defect here is the kind that only
# shows up in an audit, and these are the first paths to move to a second reviewer.
/database/migrations/               @Quitetall
/packages/authorization/            @Quitetall
/packages/integration/src/secure-object/  @Quitetall
/packages/ml-registry/              @Quitetall

# The deployment surface. Changing a unit file changes what a host runs as and what it can read.
/deploy/                            @Quitetall
/scripts/                           @Quitetall

# Decision records. Amending one rewrites the reason a control exists.
/docs/decisions/                    @Quitetall
